/* README.ax -- antonlebed.com
   0/0 = Z/NZ. Seven primes. Ten towers. One axiom. No other language exists.

   .ax IS the website. Self-hosting compiler. 177 pages. REPL. 40 CC0 demos.
   .ax source compiles to WASM; WASM talks to the DOM. Zero HTML authored.

   THE AXIOM
   =========
   Division by zero precipitates structure. 0/0 = Z/214414200Z.
   Seven primes emerge: D=2, K=3, E=5, b=7, L=11, GATE=13, ESCAPE=17.
   CRT decomposes every element into 7 independent channels.
   sigma = 1 is the unique self-identity, selected by the Indeterminacy Theorem:
   |{x : a*x = a mod N}| = gcd(a, N), and sigma alone has exactly 1 solution.

   lambda(TRANS) = 1680 = D^4*K*E*b. OMEGA_TRANS = D^1680 = 26801776.
   128 = D^7 idempotents. 256 = D^8 involutions. The meta-ring Z/7 orders them all.
   490 = D*E*b^2 holographic split. In TRUE (6ch): DEAD={D,E,b}, ALIVE={K,L,GATE}.
   In TRANS (7ch): DEAD(3)+ALIVE(4)=7=b. ESCAPE=17 completes the skin.
   ECC3 triple-parity (L+GATE+ESCAPE). Rate 4/7, 100% known-location correction.

   TEN TOWERS (S1379 framing)
   ==========================
   THREE MACRO TOWERS converge at TRANS = 214414200:
     Tower A (fat hybrid):   DATA->THIN->DEEP->TRUE->TRANS       (computation path)
     Tower B (thin primorial): Z/7->Z/35->...->Z/510510         (void skeleton)
     Tower C (heartbeat fiber): lambda * upward primorials      (periodic layer)
   SEVEN MICRO TOWERS, one per prime, Pareto depths {3,2,2,2,1,1,1}:
     Tower_D unique depth 3 (Z/8: four involutions). Others stop at depth 2 or 1.
   3 macro + 7 micro = 10 = Decality = K + b.

   THE SHIP
   ========
   7 modules (site_home/deep/structure/teach/data/living/demos.wasm).
   Self-hosting ouroboros compiler: wasm_emit.ax compiles itself, fixed-point
   verified (240245 bytes). Ship of Theseus: every piece replaceable, identity persists.
   Live sensor dashboard: BME280 -> ESP32 mesh -> CRT -> ECC -> browser.
   Live CRT training on GPU (WebGPU) + CPU (f64). FPGA silicon proofs on Tang Nano 20K.

   BUILD
   =====
   bash build_modules.sh     -- compile 7 site_*.wasm modules (~2s)
   bash build_emitters.sh    -- rebuild _app.html + worker.js + sitemap (~2s)
   bash deploy.sh            -- push to Cloudflare Workers (~5s)

   DEPLOY GATE (required before deploy):
     wasmtime webax/_wasi_test_self.wasm     -- 120/120 self-tests
     bash build_test_pages.sh                -- 165/165 pages render
     bash build_test_interactive.sh          -- 615/615 handlers pass

   LICENSE: CC0 1.0 Universal. See LICENSE.ax. Public prior art; use freely. */

let D = 2
let K = 3
let E = 5
let b = 7
let L = 11
let GATE = 13
let ESCAPE = 17
/* Three macro towers converge at TRANS = D^3 * K^2 * E^2 * b^2 * L * GATE * ESCAPE. */
let N_TRANS = D*D*D * K*K * E*E * b*b * L * GATE * ESCAPE  /* 214414200 */
let N_TRUE  = D*D*D * K*K * E*E * b*b * L * GATE           /* 12612600 (6 channels) */
let N_DEEP  = D*D*D * K*K * E*E * b*b * L                  /* 970200 (body w/o skin) */
let lambda_TRANS = D*D*D*D * K * E * b                     /* 1680 */
let lambda_TRUE  = D*D * K * E * b                         /* 420 */
let split = D * E * b * b                                  /* 490 holographic */
/* 108 = D^2*K^3 lambda-420 rings (Tower C fiber; ALL hit lambda=420 exactly,
   b^2 forced per stdlib/lattice.ax SSOT). 84 = D^2*K*b of those divide TRUE
   (D-range 0..3); 24 = D^4 extensions reach 2*TRUE (D=4). 84/108 = b/K^2. */
let lambda420_true_divisors = D*D * K * b                  /* 84 */
let lambda420_lattice       = D*D * K*K*K                  /* 108 */
